Title: Walther Lambach's Article...
subtitle: Monarchismus, People's Conservatism and Hindenburg's tower.
tags: event
new-page: true
view-if: year >= 1928 and year < 1929 and month >= 6 and weeks >= 2 and month <= 7 and dnvp_votes < 15.33 and lambach_article_seen = 0
on-arrival: lambach_article_seen = 1
face-image: img/portraits/LambachWalther.jpg

= Undisputable's Article

The publication of Walther Lambach’s latest treatise in the Politische Wochenschrift has sent a seismic shock through the foundations of the German National People’s Party. By suggesting that the shadow of the deposed Kaiser has finally been eclipsed by the towering prestige of President von Hindenburg, Lambach has enraged the national conservatives and volkists, who deemed the Walther Lambach as saboteur who would dilute the national party even further beyond the uneasy alliance of agrarians, monarchists and industrialists.

> In the future we of the German National People’s Party . . . must direct our appeal to the entire German electorate. Monarchists and republicans, join our ranks! And at the same time that we revise our attitude concern ing the form of government, we must also change our program and our party leadership. The DNVP must approach the future not as a one sided party of the past, but as a new conservative party that represents the entire nation.

>> Walther Lambach

Alfred Hugenberg has exploited the situation and launched the attack on one of biggest oppositions to his plans to eventually turn DNVP into the monolith party of radical nationalism and primarily - loyal to himself.

- @lambachfate: What will vindicate him now...?

@lambachfate
on-arrival: {!
    Q.pro_lambach = 0;
    Q.anti_lambach = 0;

    // [1] Base demographic contributions
    Q.pro_lambach += Q.workers_dnvp + Q.new_middle_dnvp + Q.unemployedc_dnvp;
    console.log("[1] pro_lambach after worker/middle/unemployed base:", Q.pro_lambach);

    Q.anti_lambach += (Q.rural_dnvp / 2.0) + (Q.old_middle_dnvp / 1.5);
    console.log("[2] anti_lambach after rural/old middle base:", Q.anti_lambach);

    // [4] CNBL crisis rural modifier
    if (Q.cnbl_crisis == 0) {
        Q.pro_lambach += Q.rural_dnvp / 10;
    };
    console.log("[4] pro_lambach after cnbl_crisis rural check:", Q.pro_lambach);

    // [5] DNVP vote threshold modifier
    if (Q.dnvp_votes > 15) {
        Q.pro_lambach += 10;
    } else if (Q.dnvp_votes > 14) {
        Q.anti_lambach += 5;
    } else {
        Q.anti_lambach += 15;
    };
    console.log("[5] pro_lambach:", Q.pro_lambach, "| anti_lambach:", Q.anti_lambach, "| after dnvp_votes check");

    // [6] Republic/nationalism/socialism modifiers
    Q.pro_lambach += Q.pro_republic / 3.5;
    console.log("[6] pro_lambach after pro_republic modifier:", Q.pro_lambach);

    Q.anti_lambach += Q.nationalism;
    console.log("[7] anti_lambach after nationalism:", Q.anti_lambach);

    if (Q.socialism < 20) {
        Q.anti_lambach += (Q.socialism / 2.5);
    };
    console.log("[8] anti_lambach after socialism check:", Q.anti_lambach);

    // [9] CNBL crisis bloc modifier
    if (Q.cnbl_crisis == 1) {
        Q.anti_lambach += 5;
    } else {
        Q.pro_lambach += 10;
    };
    console.log("[9] pro_lambach:", Q.pro_lambach, "| anti_lambach:", Q.anti_lambach, "| after cnbl_crisis bloc check");

    // [10] Combined republic/nationalism/socialism condition
    if (Q.pro_republic > 80 && Q.nationalism < 16) {
        Q.pro_lambach += 10;
    } else if (Q.pro_republic > 80 && Q.nationalism > 16) {
        Q.anti_lambach += 5;
    } else if (Q.nationalism > 20) {
        Q.anti_lambach += 10;
    } else if (Q.socialism > 20) {
        Q.pro_lambach += 10;
    } else {
        Q.anti_lambach += 20;
    };
    console.log("[10] pro_lambach:", Q.pro_lambach, "| anti_lambach:", Q.anti_lambach, "| after combined republic/nationalism/socialism block");

    // [11] Union/labor dissent modifier
    if (Q.unions_independent) {
        Q.pro_lambach += 30;
    } else if (Q.labor_dissent > 30) {
        Q.pro_lambach += Q.labor_dissent / 5;
    };
    console.log("[11] pro_lambach after union/labor dissent check:", Q.pro_lambach);

    // [12] Late-month momentum
    if (Q.month > 6) {
        Q.pro_lambach += 10;
    };
    console.log("[12] pro_lambach after month momentum check:", Q.pro_lambach);

    // [13] Final totals before binary signal
    console.log("[13] FINAL — pro_lambach:", Q.pro_lambach, "| anti_lambach:", Q.anti_lambach);

    // [14] Binary Signal Equalizer
    if (Q.pro_lambach >= Q.anti_lambach) {
        Q.lambach_exile = 0;
        Q.lambach_momentum = 1;
    } else {
        Q.lambach_exile = 1;
        Q.lambach_momentum = 0;
    };
    console.log("[14] lambach_exile:", Q.lambach_exile, "| lambach_momentum:", Q.lambach_momentum);

!}
go-to: lambach_leaves if lambach_exile = 1; lambach_stays if lambach_exile = 0

@lambach_leaves

= Lambach is expulsed!

The verdict from the regional associations is swift and merciless. Under the stern gaze of General von Dommes and the shadow of Hugenberg’s media empire, the "recalcitrant group" of fifteen provincial organizations finds its voice. They do not see a reformer; they see a "liquidator" of the Hohenzollern legacy who has traded the party’s soul for the fleeting approval of the republican masses.

​The local Potsdam association leads the charge, formally expelling Lambach for violating the party canons. While the moderate leadership under Westarp pleads for unity, the sheer weight of industrial and agrarian radicalism collapses the center. Lambach is cast out, and with him, the dream of a Volkskonservatismus withers. The DNVP hardens its heart, transforming from a broad coalition into a rigid, reactionary "Block of Stone."

[? if developer_mode = 1: [+ anti_lambach +] Anti and Pro [+ pro_lambach +] ?]

@lambach_stays

= Lambach survives the case!

In a surprising display of resilience, the "community of interests" holds firm against the radical onslaught. The Party Court renders a verdict of acquittal, declaring that Lambach’s intention was not to destroy the monarchy, but to preserve the nation’s future through healthy debate.

​[? if unions_independent : The surging independence of the trade unions has made Lambach's presence a tactical necessity that even the Junkers cannot ignore. ?] [? if socialism > 20 : A growing social consciousness within the ranks has provided the 'Christian Social' faction with the leverage needed to shield their leader. ?]

​Lambach remains, his position as the voice of the workers' wing significantly fortified. However, this victory is a bitter one; Hugenberg and his Pan-German allies withdraw into a state of "excellent fighting mood," preparing a final, decisive coup for the October Congress.

[? if developer_mode = 1: [+ anti_lambach +] Anti and Pro [+ pro_lambach +] ?]
